# ---- Dirty : dirty-cell masks, board restore from the background -------------
# Per displayed buffer, 13 row words; word r+1 bit c+1 = board cell (c,r) must be
# copied back from the background buffer before sprites are drawn again.
F_143d6 Dirty_Init
@Dirty_Init Dirty_Init() : point gDirtyMaskPtr / gDirtyCurCursorRect at the first buffer's data.
F_143ea Dirty_Reset
@Dirty_Reset Dirty_Reset() : mark every cell dirty on both buffers and forget the cursor
@Dirty_Reset rectangles (round start, after the spinner).
F_14426 Dirty_DeInit
@Dirty_DeInit Dirty_DeInit() : clear both masks.
F_14458 Dirty_RestoreBoard
@Dirty_RestoreBoard Dirty_RestoreBoard() : for the logic buffer, copy every dirty board cell from the
@Dirty_RestoreBoard background (F_16604), then the 32x16 block under the saved puzzle cursor.
F_1454c Dirty_RestoreCell
@Dirty_RestoreCell Dirty_RestoreCell(d0 = row, d1 = column) : copy one 16x16 board cell from the
@Dirty_RestoreCell background to the logic screen.
F_145b8 Dirty_RestoreWrapColumn
@Dirty_RestoreWrapColumn Dirty_RestoreWrapColumn() : restore the dirty cells of the column left of
@Dirty_RestoreWrapColumn the board (x=112, sprites wrapping around) and select this buffer's mask.
F_14600 Dirty_MarkCell
@Dirty_MarkCell Dirty_MarkCell(d0 = bit, d1 = word) : set a bit in the current mask (raw
@Dirty_MarkCell coordinates: bit = column+1, word = row+1).
F_1461a Dirty_SetCursorRect
@Dirty_SetCursorRect Dirty_SetCursorRect(a0 = cursor) : remember the cursor position so that
@Dirty_SetCursorRect Dirty_RestoreBoard restores the block under it (puzzle cursor).
F_1463c Dirty_MarkSprite
@Dirty_MarkSprite Dirty_MarkSprite(a0 = object, +0 x, +4 y in 20.12 fixed point) : mark the 1 to 4
@Dirty_MarkSprite cells covered by a 16x16 sprite at that position.
F_146d8 Dirty_MarkSpriteCentred
@Dirty_MarkSpriteCentred Dirty_MarkSpriteCentred(a0 = object) : same, the position being the sprite
@Dirty_MarkSpriteCentred centre (8 pixels subtracted first).
F_14780 Dirty_InvalidateAll
@Dirty_InvalidateAll Dirty_InvalidateAll() : mark every cell dirty on both buffers.
